This is a collection of YANIs by users of the #nethack IRC channel on
freenode.net. Please excuse any old ideas that may be present.

[1]: Monster: Adventurer - well, actually, this already exists in the
game in the form of valkyries, and other @'s that I think you only ever
see if you STF a bones-file statue. Well, why not have random
adventurers in the dungeon with you? Some hostile, some peaceful. All
of them scooping up treasure if you don't get to it first. --azgor

[2]: You should be able to burn Elbereth with a potion of acid. --Thvor

[3]: While standing on or in water, dipping (or perhaps engraving with)
a wand of lightning should have the effect of electrocuting nearby
monsters (and possibly you). --aioli

[4]: The Book should be readable in Braille to simplify the description
(and future official implementation) of the zen conduct. --aioli

[5]: There should be a #call command, to avoid the need for a prompt in
#name. --SimonRC

[6]: There should be a chance of catching a thrown potion based on
dexterity. This chance could never excede 50% though to account for
potions thrown at you from behind.  One would never be able to catch a
potion thrown by an unseen monster.  --azgor

[7]: There should be a command called "pour" which allows you to dump
out a potion and keep the empty bottle. Might also be used for ID
purposes? --Dragonmaw

[8]: How's this instead of my idea from last time: turn undead causes
humans to turn into L,M,V,W,Z or ghosts, or shades; and
k,G,o,dwarves,elves,ettins,and giants to turn into their respective M's
or Z's. --azgor

[9]: Anti-gravity: You can gain it by boots of such, or a potion of
such. It basically gives you flying, and the ability to kick objects
and bounce without dying. It also gives you control of your movement on
the Plane of Air. --TheShrewdDude

[10]: Wading: Large enough creatures should be able to just walk into
pools and use them, much like creatures with the ability to swim.
--TheShrewdDude

[11]: Infravision Goggles: Grant you infravision, if you don't have it
already. Appearance: a pair of lenses. --TheShrewdDude

[12]: Valkyries should start with a tame wolf and they should be able
to ride wolves as per Norse mythology.  Either that or they should have
wings and be able to fly as per popular corruption of Norse mythology.
--azgor

[13]: Looking at a monster (with ; or /) should tell you if it is
noticably asleep, paralyzed, or fleeing. --Thvor

[14]: Uranium wands should have some amusing property. Perhaps
engraving causes the bugs on the floor to glow in addition to the
normal behavior. --azgor

[15]: If prayer uncurses a worn blindfold, it should produce a message
to show that it was uncursed. --NESoutlaw_


